    {
      "id": "txt010",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 190,
      "width": 427.8,
      "height": 168.75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 79190,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1047290,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Seven values have nowhere to go, so seven\nof them get an address on the stack instead\nof a register. That is spilling, and it is not\na bug or a failure. It is the only answer\navailable once the counting comes out that\nway.\n\nSame source on aarch64, which hands out 30,\nand nothing spills at all.",
      "originalText": "Seven values have nowhere to go, so seven\nof them get an address on the stack instead\nof a register. That is spilling, and it is not\na bug or a failure. It is the only answer\navailable once the counting comes out that\nway.\n\nSame source on aarch64, which hands out 30,\nand nothing spills at all.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "txt011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 591.48,
      "height": 22.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 87109,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1152019,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Why the counting is per point and not per function",
      "originalText": "2. Why the counting is per point and not per function",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "txt012",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 460,
      "width": 1081.28,
      "height": 40.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 95028,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1256748,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Two values only compete if they are both alive at the same instant. A function with a hundred variables in it\nneeds two registers if only two of them are ever live together. The unit is the live range, not the variable.",
      "originalText": "Two values only compete if they are both alive at the same instant. A function with a hundred variables in it\nneeds two registers if only two of them are ever live together. The unit is the live range, not the variable.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
